  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the security of threatened wildlife and their habitat through the local empowerment in the Ancestral Rainforest Landscape, Selva Maya, Guatemala</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) give continuity to the implementation of the Hunting Region II Socialization Program to empowerindigenous authorities and establish consensual agreements that favor conservation, security and management of wildlife and their habitat in communities of Ixcn, Quich that are key to the landscape connectivity; 2) promote a pilot process to empower local youth featured as leaders of change acting for wildlife and social welfare; 3) enable an intercultural experimental space that benefits the training of local youth in good practices of conservation and sustainable productivity with the potential to be promoted to larger scale; and 4) evaluate the impact of the process by monitoring social indicators and ecological in the study regions.</narrative>
  </description>
